# Remote Air Service — business rules (source of truth)

**Read before implementing:** `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_CONTEXT_FOR_NEW_FEATURES.md` · `docs/NEW_FEATURES_COMPARISON.md` · `docs/FUNCTIONALITY_WIRING_PLAN.md`

This is a **marketplace + membership + remote aviation reputation** platform. Preserve dark aviation UI; align behavior to client PDFs.

## Commission

- Default **15%** platform commission (not 10%). Not tier-based by default.
- Super Admin per-pilot override — future (not in schema yet).
- A-4+ commission buyout — post-launch only.

## Membership

- **$99.99/year** for all pilots (base membership).
- A-2–A-6 = **one-time Fast Forward upgrade fees** — NOT monthly tier subscriptions.
- Later upgrade charges **difference only** (new fee − prior fee paid).
- Instructor add-on: **$199.99/year**, min grade A-4.
- Lapse: grade time stops, benefits/verification inactive.
- Profile delete: warn user; **30-day reactivation** retains grade.

## Grades & visibility

- A-1 Student → A-6 Captain (A-7–A-10 later, invitation only).
- Visibility after admin approval: 48h / 36h / 24h / 12h / 6h / 0h.
- **A-1 cannot submit proposals.** A-2+ can when visible.

## Marketplace flow

Client post → admin approve → grade-based visibility → pilot proposal → client review → **client initiates chat** → revision max **+20%** → booking/contract → escrow → deliver → approve → payout minus 15% → ratings/awards.

## Separate systems

- **Messages** — client/pilot; admin read-only tracking (no staff composer).
- **Support Chat** — real support (keep as-is).
- **Disputes** — formal workflow; no ratings/awards until resolved.

## Out of scope now

- Stripe / escrow implementation unless task explicitly requests it.
- Remote Rescue (late 2027).
- Squadron Vote dispute escalation (post-MVP).
- Final certificate font assets (client TBD).

## Registration (unchanged)

M02 register: email, password, role only. Extended fields via onboarding (M03/M04).

## Figma

Client updated Figma — reconcile with these rules before visual changes; prefer token-based updates.
